        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-updates" data-main="software" data-sub="updates">
            <div class="info">
                The winget updater <strong>configuration</strong>: master switch, the device groups that are updated
                automatically, the ignore list and the run log. Nothing runs automatically until you enable it here
                <strong>and</strong> tick at least one group; automatic runs follow a two-stage policy (right after a
                device connects on a day it has not been updated yet, otherwise at the latest 24 h after its previous
                run - no interval to configure). Updates are silent, one package at a time, and never reboot a device;
                ignored packages are skipped and optionally pinned on the client, so even a manual
                <code>winget upgrade --all</code> leaves license-bound versions alone. Devices without winget are
                reported per run, offline devices are skipped, and the log keeps one line per package.
                <br><br>
                The per-device actions live on the rows of <em>Devices &gt; Device list</em>, the per-package fleet
                actions on the rows of <em>Software &gt; Software list</em> - every button explains itself on hover.
                Changes on this page are saved the moment they happen.
            </div>

            <div class="controls">
                <label data-help="wg.save"><input type="checkbox" id="wgEnabled"> Enable automatic winget updates</label>
                <label><input type="checkbox" id="wgPinSync"> Pin ignored packages on clients</label>

                <button id="wgSaveBtn" data-help="wg.save">Save Configuration</button>
                <button id="wgRunBtn" class="green" data-help="wg.run">Run Now</button>
                <button id="wgDryAllBtn" data-help="wg.dryall">Dry run all devices</button>
                <span id="wgRunState" class="hint"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="hint">Every change on this page (switches, groups, ignore list) is saved immediately; the
            "Save Configuration" button re-applies the whole form explicitly. Excluding a single device is done on
            its row in the device list and is saved atomically - it never rewrites this form.</div>

            <h3>Device groups to update automatically</h3>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th style="width:120px;">Auto-update</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="wgGroupBody"><tr><td colspan="2" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
            </table></div>

            <h3>Ignore list (never auto-upgrade these package ids)</h3>
            <div class="controls">
                <input id="wgIgId" type="text" placeholder="package id, e.g. Adobe.Acrobat.Reader.64-bit" style="min-width:280px;">
                <input id="wgIgNote" type="text" placeholder="reason (optional: license pinned to v11)" style="min-width:240px;">
                <button id="wgIgAdd" data-help="swf.ignore">Add</button>
            </div>
            <div class="table-container"><table>
                <thead><tr><th style="width:320px;">Package id</th><th>Note</th><th style="width:80px;"></th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="wgIgBody"></tbody>
            </table></div>
            <div id="wgMsg"></div>

            <h3>Update log</h3>
            <div><button id="refreshWgLogBtn" class="small">Refresh log</button> <span id="wgLogInfo" class="hint"></span></div>
            <pre id="wgLog" style="max-height:260px;overflow:auto;background:#0f1720;color:#cfe3f5;padding:8px;border-radius:6px;font-size:11px;margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;">(not loaded yet)</pre>
        </div>
